", "watch": "A sharp national Republican wave or unexpectedly low Democratic turnout in Chicago and the collar counties could compress the margin, though not enough to threaten the outcome.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent JB Pritzker (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor JB Pritzker seeks a third term against state senator Darren Bailey, whom he defeated by double digits in 2022. Illinois leans Democratic by about six points, and Pritzker's incumbency, fundraising dominance, and high profile add to that edge. Every major race rater places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets price Pritzker's chances near 98 percent.\n\nLate polls from Research Co., ActiVote, and Public Policy Polling show Pritzker leading by 16 to 20 points among likely voters, with the most recent survey ending just before Election Day. Bailey has struggled to broaden his appeal beyond his downstate base, and outside spending has not closed the gap. The forecast expects a comfortable Pritzker win, with residual uncertainty reflecting normal polling and turnout variation rather than genuine competitive risk.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.98, "margin": 13.88}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 13.9}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9823, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9788, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9803, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9741, "ma